  "text": "cc-track context window pressure points:\n- System patterns file is comprehensive but maybe too detailed for every session\n- Decision log grows over time and is always loaded\n- Spec folders contain multiple files (spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, progress.md) all loaded\n- Active task context includes full git diffs during review\n\nThe spec-driven workflow actually makes this worse in some ways:\n- More structured documentation = more tokens per feature\n- Separation of concerns (good for clarity) = more files to load (bad for context)\n- Constitution + clarification + planning = thorough but verbose\n\nPotential optimizations:\n1. Lazy-load decision log (only relevant entries, not full file)\n2. Compress system_patterns into concise rules\n3. Context tiers: Always-load vs On-demand\n4. Store more state externally (logs, reviews) rather than in-context\n5. Explicit session boundaries with state checkpoints",
  "sections": [
    "Project Notes"
  ],
